From: Galaxy Book 12 Linux contributors
Subject: [PATCH] media: ipu-bridge: add Galaxy Book 12 cameras

The Samsung Galaxy Book 12 exposes its rear Sony IMX258 as SONY258A and its
front Sony IMX241 as INT347F. Without entries in ipu_supported_sensors,
ipu-bridge does not attach the software-node graph and sensor probe fails with
"Endpoint node not found".

The patched IMX258 driver provides the exact 650 and 321.75 MHz link
frequencies found in Samsung's official 26 MHz sensor tables.

--- a/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
+++ b/drivers/media/pci/intel/ipu-bridge.c
@@ -99,2 +99,6 @@
 	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("OVTI8856", 3, 180000000, 360000000, 720000000),
+	/* Sony IMX241 (Samsung Galaxy Book 12 front camera) */
+	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("INT347F", 1, 360966667),
+	/* Sony IMX258 (Samsung Galaxy Book 12) */
+	IPU_SENSOR_CONFIG("SONY258A", 2, 650000000, 321750000),
 	/* Sony IMX471 */
